   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## hy3d-full-workflow.json\n\nHy3D shape -> texture\n\n**Does:** image -> 3D mesh -> texture -> bake, with Hunyuan3D 2.x.\n**View:** both exports end in a `Preview3D` node \u2014 orbit them in the canvas (textures render since core v0.46 / frontend 1.59.6 - tested 2026-11-19) \u2014 plus a **Textured turntable (12 frames)**:\n`Hy3DNvdiffrastRenderer` renders the textured mesh through a full 360\u00b0 as an image batch, which is the\nreliable way to see the texture.\n**Note:** the untextured export is the **retopologised** shape (`Hy3DIMRemesh`) and the textured GLB\nis the final \u2014 so the shape checkpoint is the one to rig or bring into an engine.\n**PBR:** the bake is base colour only, so the flow also writes the atlas as an image\n(`3D/Hy3D_texture_atlas_*`) - feed it to `2d/workflows/pbr-material.json` to get\nBaseColor/Normal/Roughness/Metallic/ORM for an engine.\n**See:** `3d/README.md`, `3d/pipeline-design.md`, and the widget reference in `3d/hy3d-knobs.md`.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S12** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E2a-e** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## hy3d-full-workflow.json\n\nHy3D shape -> texture\n\n**Does:** image -> 3D mesh -> texture -> bake, with Hunyuan3D 2.x.\n**View:** both exports end in a `Preview3D` node \u2014 orbit them in the canvas (geometry only: the\nviewer renders no textures on the current frontend) \u2014 plus a **Textured turntable (12 frames)**:\n`Hy3DNvdiffrastRenderer` renders the textured mesh through a full 360\u00b0 as an image batch, which is the\nreliable way to see the texture.\n**Note:** the untextured export is the **retopologised** shape (`Hy3DIMRemesh`) and the textured GLB\nis the final \u2014 so the shape checkpoint is the one to rig or bring into an engine.\n**PBR:** the bake is base colour only, so the flow also writes the atlas as an image\n(`3D/Hy3D_texture_atlas_*`) - feed it to `2d/workflows/pbr-material.json` to get\nBaseColor/Normal/Roughness/Metallic/ORM for an engine.\n**See:** `3d/README.md`, `3d/pipeline-design.md`, and the widget reference in `3d/hy3d-knobs.md`.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S12** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E2a-e** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   },
   "color": "#332922",
   "bgcolor": "#593930"
  },
